// One micro-finding (n1 here, distinct from the org-audit n1):
// the audit-history/*.oot files use 4-element Academy header
// (`// # Title\n//\n// Logline: ...`) but the .oot extension.
// RULES.oot §1.19 expects 2-element Markdown (# Title / File:) on
// .oot. The audit-history/ANCHOR.oo sets the precedent; my
// 2026-09-10 audit (this file) follows it. This is a precedent
// pattern, not a violation — but it's worth noting because
// governance_enforce.oo Rule B would catch the audit-history/
// files if scoped to .oo extension. NOT a finding.

